No. In development, Strict Mode intentionally runs an extra **setup → cleanup → setup** cycle to stress-test your Effect and reveal missing cleanup logic; production runs the initial setup only once.[1][3]

Write the Effect so its cleanup fully mirrors and undoes its setup—for example:

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const connection = createConnection(serverUrl, roomId);
  connection.connect();

  return () => {
    connection.disconnect();
  };
}, [roomId]);
```

The cleanup disconnects the previous connection before the Effect runs again and when the component unmounts.[3][8] Include reactive values such as `roomId` in the dependency array so the Effect reconnects when they change.[9] Don’t use a ref merely to suppress the second run, because that leaves connections open across remounts.[2]

